The attached image illustrates the active transport and distribution of Nano-11 nanoparticles within the draining lymph nodes following intramuscular injection. Panel A and B show that the percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells peaks on Day 2 post-injection, decreasing significantly by Day 7. Panel C details the distribution among APC subtypes, revealing that Migratory Dendritic Cells (MigDCs) consistently account for the largest proportion of Nano-11-positive cells. Panel D further indicates that MigDCs exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity of Nano-11, signifying a greater per-cell uptake compared to Lymphoid Tissue Resident DCs (LTDCs) and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ).